    {
      "text": "The Al-free equiatomic FeCoNi baseline is single-phase FCC.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Single-phase FCC FeCoNi-based alloys typically have coercive fields no greater than approximately 100 Oe.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding approximately 5–10 at.% Al to equiatomic FeCoNi and annealing near 1050 °C followed by rapid quenching will produce partial B2 ordering or a B2-type secondary phase.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed ordered regions or secondary phase will occur within an FCC/BCC matrix.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A two-phase microstructure can have higher coercivity than a single-phase microstructure in FeCoNi-based alloys.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9079992::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Localized B2-like ordering or a B2-type secondary phase pins magnetic domain walls.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Domain-wall pinning caused by the ordered phase increases coercivity.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed Al addition and heat treatment will raise room-temperature coercivity above 100 Oe.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy will maintain high saturation magnetization relative to single-phase FeCoNi or a closely matched derivative.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Annealing can substantially influence the magnetic properties of FeCoNi-based compositionally complex alloys.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9079992::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting coercivity will depend on Al concentration and heat-treatment parameters.",
